          <p>France offers some of Europe's finest dark skies, particularly across the Massif Central, Provence, and the Pyrenees. The Cévennes National Park holds France's first International Dark Sky Reserve designation, with Bortle 2–3 skies over its granite plateaux. Southern France benefits from 300+ clear nights per year in favourable areas, and high-altitude sites like the Pic du Midi Observatory (2877m) in the Pyrenees provide exceptional atmospheric transparency. The best viewing period is May through October, with autumn offering the ideal balance of clear skies and comfortable temperatures.</p>
